### IDOR Enforcement Pattern (Change #3)

Every endpoint that touches a resource follows this chain:

```python
async def get_scan_findings(scan_id: str, current_user: User = Depends(get_current_user), db: Session = Depends(get_db)):
    scan = db.query(Scan).filter(Scan.id == scan_id).first()
    if not scan:
        raise HTTPException(404)
    repo = db.query(Repository).filter(Repository.id == scan.repo_id).first()
    if repo.user_id != current_user.id:      # ← IDOR check
        raise HTTPException(403)
    ...
```

A `get_owned_scan(scan_id, user)` helper will be shared across all routers.

