## 8. Patch Guardrails (Change #12)

`patch_validator.py` rejects any LLM-generated fix that violates:

| Check | Rule |
|---|---|
| **File scope** | `fix.file` must exactly equal `finding.file_path` |
| **Path traversal** | Resolved path must be inside `workspace_dir`; no `..` segments; symlinks ignored |
| **Protected files** | Reject if file matches: `.github/workflows/**`, `Dockerfile*`, `*.lock`, `package.json`, `*.cfg` CI configs |
| **Lockfiles** | Reject `package-lock.json`, `yarn.lock`, `Pipfile.lock`, `poetry.lock` |
| **Scripts** | Reject if `package.json:scripts.*` would be modified |
| **Patch size** | Diff line count ≤ `MAX_PATCH_LINES` (default 200) |
| **Line bounds** | `line_start` ≥ 1, `line_end` ≤ file line count, `line_start ≤ line_end` |

Any violation is a hard reject — the fix attempt is marked failed and fed back to the Fix node.

