## 9. Sandbox Architecture (Changes #13, #14, #15)

### Two-Stage Design

```
Stage A — install (network: bridge, cpu: 1.0, mem: 1g, timeout: 300s)
  Input:  workspace (read-write bind mount, scoped to scan workspace dir)
  Action: pip install -r requirements.txt  OR  npm ci
  Output: workspace with installed deps (committed to a Docker volume)
  Notes:  No secrets injected. Install scripts are untrusted; run only here.

Stage B — scan+test (network: none, cpu: 0.5, mem: 512m, timeout: 120s)
  Input:  workspace from Stage A (read-only) + /tmp (writable)
  Action: semgrep --config /rules --metrics=off  + pytest / npm test
  Output: JSON results written to /tmp/results/
  Notes:  Non-root user (uid 1000), no new privileges, seccomp default profile.
```

### Docker Socket

FastAPI backend (trusted) spawns sandbox containers via the Docker SDK. **The Docker socket is NOT bind-mounted into any sandbox container.** Sandbox containers have no ability to create other containers.

### Scanner Image Build (Change #14)

```dockerfile
FROM python:3.11-slim AS sandbox
# Bundle Semgrep rules at build time — never use --config auto in offline stage
COPY docker/sandbox/rules/ /rules/
RUN pip install semgrep==1.x.x --no-cache-dir
RUN useradd -u 1000 -m scanner
USER scanner
```

### Clone Hygiene (Change #16)

```python
env = {
    "GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM": "1",
    "HOME": "/dev/null",          # prevent reading ~/.gitconfig
    "GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT": "0",
}
cmd = [
    "git", "clone",
    "--depth=1",
    "--no-local",
    "--config", "core.hooksPath=/dev/null",  # disable hooks
    "--no-recurse-submodules",
    f"--config", f"http.extraHeader=Authorization: Bearer {token}",
    repo_url,
    workspace_dir,
]
# After clone: unset remote URL to purge token from .git/config
subprocess.run(["git", "remote", "set-url", "origin", ""], cwd=workspace_dir)
```

Workspace deletion:
```python
try:
    run_scan(state)
finally:
    shutil.rmtree(workspace_dir, ignore_errors=True)
```

TTL cleanup job runs on a schedule and deletes any `{WORKSPACE_ROOT}/scans/{scan_id}` directories older than `SCAN_TIMEOUT_TOTAL`.

